cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use numgrids in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "numgrids: Working with numerical grids made easy"
abstract: >-
  numgrids is a Python package for numerical grids in any dimension and in
  curvilinear coordinates, with spectral and finite-difference
  differentiation, integration, interpolation, vector calculus, boundary
  conditions, and solvers for boundary value, eigenvalue and time-dependent
  problems.
authors:
  - family-names: Baer
    given-names: Matthias
repository-code: "https://github.com/maroba/numgrids"
url: "https://maroba.github.io/numgrids/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - numerical grids
  - spectral methods
  - finite differences
  - partial differential equations
  - curvilinear coordinates
